 while, the truth was brutal.\\n\\nRemember the MIT study that found 95% of generative AI pilots never delivered measurable ROI? Well, it made the rounds, and the AI hype curve dipped.\\n\\nBut something shifted in 2025 when agentic AI moved from buzzword to real deployment.\\n\\nWe recently commissioned a study with CMP Research to survey customer contact, customer experience, and operations leaders running agentic AI in production today.\\n\\nThe headline finding? 96% say agentic AI met or exceeded their ROI expectations.\\n\\nThat\\u2019s a complete inversion of the MIT findings on GenAI pilots.\\n\\nWith agentic AI, enterprises are actually getting the return they were promised, and it\\u2019s because the platforms for building powerful AI agents have finally caught up to the vision.\\n\\nTake OASYS, our Orchestrated Agent System at SoundHound AI. Simply describe the agent you want, connect your data, and it builds the optimal agents for your business.\\n\\nIt feels like Tony Stark and J.A.R.V.I.S.: Stark sets the direction, and J.A.R.V.I.S. takes the action. Except agentic AI isn\\u2019t movie magic. It\\u2019s real tech in production today, and it couldn\\u2019t have arrived at a better time.\\n\\nFor decades, the collective sentiment was that customer service automation = frustration. Chatbots, IVR systems, and even GenAI agents trained us to just ask for a human if we wanted to get anything meaningful done.\\n\\nAgentic AI has flipped the script. Not only is it easier than ever to build AI agents, those agents are delivering the results that enterprises (and their customers) expect.\\n\\nOur new report has all the insights you\\u2019ll want to know: \\n\\nI\\u2019ll also be at #CCWVegas next week, booth #756, and would love to talk about what this research means for your CX operation. Be sure to stop by if you\\u2019re attending!\\" \\/><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\"lan-ad__additional-hidden-content\\"><script src=\\"https:\\/\\/sonar.script.ac\\/c739218\\/c